    {
      "id": "thukjqg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PARLIAMENT OF INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Parliament of India comprises the President, Lok Sabha (House of the People), and Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Rajya Sabha is a permanent body not subject to dissolution, while Lok Sabha has a standard tenure of 5 years unless dissolved earlier.",
        "Money Bills can originate only in the Lok Sabha with the prior consent of the President.",
        "Joint Sessions are summoned by the President to resolve deadlocks on Ordinary Bills and are presided over by the Lok Sabha Speaker.",
        "Disqualification under the Anti-Defection Law is governed by the 10th Schedule and decided by the Presiding Officer of the respective House."
      ],
      "id": "ysuam0s"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
