    },
    {
      "id": "u14o9w7",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>INTRODUCTION</strong>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "99s4joo",
      "content": "The Parliament of India is the supreme legislative body of the country."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sdlmr9c",
      "content": "It represents the will of the people and plays a crucial role in law-making, governance, and control over the executive."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rulksel",
      "content": "The Parliament of India is mentioned in Part V (Articles 79–122) of the Indian Constitution. It is the backbone of Indian democracy."
    },
    {
      "id": "tz2ros4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "COMPOSITION OF THE PARLIAMENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "oyncwf9",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "en92n3o",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_en92n3o.gif"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gd5busd",
      "content": "According to Article 79, the Parliament consists of: "
    },
    {
      "id": "obl9aar",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>The President of India</li><li>Lok Sabha (House of the People)</li><li>Rajya Sabha (Council of States)</li></ul>",
        "The President of India",
        "Lok Sabha (House of the People)",
        "Rajya Sabha (Council of States)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9glksa4",
      "content": "The President is an integral part of Parliament, even though he/she is not a member of either House."
    },
    {
      "id": "dgkduaw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LOK SABHA – HOUSE OF THE PEOPLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zipqb4e",
      "content": "Lok Sabha is the lower house and the real legislative authority. Composition:"
    },
    {
      "id": "gmndfge",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Maximum strength – 552 members</li><li>Present strength – 543 elected members</li><li>Members are directly elected by the people</li><li>Term – 5 years (unless dissolved earlier)</li></ul>",
        "Maximum strength – 552 members",
        "Present strength – 543 elected members",
        "Members are directly elected by the people",
        "Term – 5 years (unless dissolved earlier)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zwu029r",
      "content": "Qualifications:"
    },
    {
      "id": "1djd40m",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Citizen of India</li><li>Minimum age – 25 years</li><li>Must not hold an office of profit</li></ul>",
        "Citizen of India",
        "Minimum age – 25 years",
        "Must not hold an office of profit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5hjoq1r",
      "content": "Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "wxj2vk6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Controls the executive</li><li>Money Bills originate here</li><li>No-Confidence Motion can be introduced</li><li>Final authority over finances</li></ul>",
        "Controls the executive",
        "Money Bills originate here",
        "No-Confidence Motion can be introduced",
        "Final authority over finances"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lptdgy3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RAJYA SABHA – COUNCIL OF STATES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gbuyw8h",
      "content": "Rajya Sabha is the upper house and represents states and union territories. Composition:"
    },
    {
      "id": "20l62ui",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Maximum strength – 250</li><li>Present strength – 245</li><li>Members are indirectly elected</li><li>12 members nominated by President (arts, science, literature)</li></ul>",
        "Maximum strength – 250",
        "Present strength – 245",
        "Members are indirectly elected",
        "12 members nominated by President (arts, science, literature)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "op4qmwe",
      "content": "Term:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ddnynvs",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Permanent House</li><li>One-third members retire every two years</li></ul>",
        "Permanent House",
        "One-third members retire every two years"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jim0ith",
      "content": "Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ous9dl",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Revising and delaying legislation</li><li>Protects federal interests</li><li>Can initiate non-money bills</li></ul>",
        "Revising and delaying legislation",
        "Protects federal interests",
        "Can initiate non-money bills"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bmk1t65",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PRESIDENT AS PART OF PARLIAMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "on2w8g7",
      "content": "The President is an integral part of Parliament. Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "wx0tedy",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Summons and prorogues Parliament</li><li>Dissolves Lok Sabha</li><li>Addresses joint sessions</li><li>Gives assent to bills</li><li>Issues ordinances during recess</li></ul>",
        "Summons and prorogues Parliament",
        "Dissolves Lok Sabha",
        "Addresses joint sessions",
        "Gives assent to bills",
        "Issues ordinances during recess"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4vkuj2o",
      "content": "Without President‟s assent, no bill becomes law."
    },
    {
      "id": "6tqb6om",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SESSIONS OF PARLIAMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "17zxj83",
      "content": "Parliament meets in three sessions:"
    },
    {
      "id": "hkn8t5n",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Budget Session (Feb–May)</li><li>Monsoon Session (July–August)</li><li>Winter Session (Nov–Dec)</li></ul>",
        "Budget Session (Feb–May)",
        "Monsoon Session (July–August)",
        "Winter Session (Nov–Dec)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lntxvz9",
      "content": "There should not be a gap of more than 6 months between two sessions."
    },
    {
      "id": "g7rfm9l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "QUORUM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8sa12xq",
      "content": "Quorum is the minimum number of members required to conduct a meeting. Quorum = 1/10th of total membership of the House."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oa6le7f",
      "content": "If quorum is not present, the House is adjourned."
    },
    {
      "id": "634snp4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LAW MAKING PROCEDURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9sih136",
      "content": "Ordinary Bill:"
    },
    {
      "id": "4siitv2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Introduced in either House</li><li>Passed by both Houses</li><li>President‟s assent required</li></ul>",
        "Introduced in either House",
        "Passed by both Houses",
        "President‟s assent required"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bgavilc",
      "content": "Money Bill:"
    },
    {
      "id": "4o4g7r5",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Introduced only in Lok Sabha</li><li>Rajya Sabha can only make recommendations</li><li>Passed within 14 days</li></ul>",
        "Introduced only in Lok Sabha",
        "Rajya Sabha can only make recommendations",
        "Passed within 14 days"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "927hgqn",
      "content": "Constitutional Amendment Bill:"
    },
    {
      "id": "qwugd2s",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Special majority required</li><li>Some require ratification by states</li></ul>",
        "Special majority required",
        "Some require ratification by states"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ysvqz9o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MONEY BILL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1pwvyce",
      "content": "A Money Bill deals with:"
    },
    {
      "id": "thbk730",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Taxes</li><li>Borrowing of money</li><li>Consolidated Fund</li><li>Expenditure of government</li></ul>",
        "Taxes",
        "Borrowing of money",
        "Consolidated Fund",
        "Expenditure of government"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ofi5omn",
      "content": "Certification:"
    },
    {
      "id": "u9mo9yg",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Certified by the Speaker of Lok Sabha</li><li>Decision of Speaker is final</li></ul>",
        "Certified by the Speaker of Lok Sabha",
        "Decision of Speaker is final"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8aqujb5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "JOINT SESSION OF PARLIAMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h0v6cyu",
      "content": "Joint Session is called to resolve deadlock between two Houses. Presided by: Speaker of Lok Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vzhzwmk",
      "content": "Cases where joint session is not allowed:"
    },
